==Sailing Changes==
We also have a batch of Sailing adjustments lined up for you, focused on making looting more efficient. Firstly, Herb Sack, Seed Box and Rune Pouch now all work with looting Sailing creatures. Note that for this to work:

* Herb Sack and Seed Box must be open.
* Rune-picking behaviour toggle must be enabled in the Settings, so that the looted runes can be put inside the Rune Pouch if there's already a matching stack of that rune for them to join.

Additionally, to make creating cannonballs at the Ancient Furnace more convenient, we’ve added a new NPC, Isles, who can be found wandering outside the bank at Port Roberts. If you've sailed to Grimstone before, speak to Isles and invite him to accompany you there on your boat. Once you enter the Grimstone Dungeon, he'll become available at the Ancient Furnace. There, he can unnote any metal bar that's used for making cannonballs, charging 100 coins per note.

[[File:Further Leagues VI Changes (3).png|thumb|500px|center|''If you can’t see the image above, click [https://cdn.runescape.com/assets/img/external/oldschool/2026/Newsposts/2026-05-06/isles.png here]!'']]

Moreover, casting Telekinetic Grab on defeated seaborne creatures now lets you collect their loot while remaining engaged to the cannon, or to similar facilities on your boat such as the Salvaging Hook and Trawling Net. Your character will cast the spell and will get right back to the cannon without needing to re-click the cannon again. In a similar vein, Telekinetic Grab now works on Lost Crates too, provided you have the required Sailing level and some space for the crates' contents.

